# External library suppressions for ThreadSanitizer (P0-28 audited minimal set)
# 1. System libQt6Core.so is compiled without TSan instrumentation; its internal atomic refcounting
#    (QArrayData/QString COW) and futex-based QBasicMutex/QWaitCondition are invisible to TSan.
#    Note: Desk32's audio engine (pipeline, DSP, mailbox, SPSC queue, reclaimer, decoder, decks)
#    uses pure C++20 stdtypes and passes TSan with this rule removed.
race:libQt6Core.so
# 2. Qt6 QTest Watchdog thread internal stack variable race during QTest::qExec teardown
race:libQt6Test
# 3. Qt6 QTest Watchdog QThread leak at process exit (Desk32 uses std::thread exclusively)
thread:QThread::start
# 4. PipeWire pw_thread_loop internal mutex unlock across loop/control threads
mutex:libpipewire-0.3.so
